  {%- case gem_handle -%}
    {%- when 'emerald' -%}
      <div class="gem-care">
        <p>Emerald has a delicate internal structure. It is not fragile, but it is naturally more sensitive than harder stones like Sapphire. That inner life — its inclusions, its softness of glow, its living texture — is part of what makes it valuable. Mindful care keeps it stable, beautiful, and wearable for years.</p>
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 16px;">
          <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a3c34; margin-bottom: 10px;">Do</h4>
            <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
              <li>Clean gently with a soft cloth after wear.</li>
              <li>Use lukewarm water and a drop of mild soap occasionally.</li>
              <li>Store separately in a padded box to prevent knocks from harder stones.</li>
              <li>If professionally advised, light colourless oil maintenance may be done when appropriate.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div style="background: #fff5f5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h4 style="color: #c53030; margin-bottom: 10px;">Avoid</h4>
            <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
              <li>Heat, steam, sudden temperature shifts.</li>
              <li>Ultrasonic cleaning.</li>
              <li>Harsh chemicals, perfumes, detergents, and alcohol-based products.</li>
              <li>Remove during gym sessions, heavy physical activity, or situations where impact is likely.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 16px; border-left: 4px solid var(--color-gold); margin-top: 20px;">
          <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>On treatments:</strong> Light to moderate colourless oiling is a globally accepted and traditional practice for Emeralds, and it should always be fully disclosed on certification. What is never acceptable — and what we never carry — is heavy resin, polymer, wax, or glass filling disguised as quality. Visible oil seepage, suspicious clarity, or an unnaturally “perfect” appearance are all signs to look closer.</p>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top: 16px;">Handled gently, Emerald holds its colour, composure, and quiet brilliance for a lifetime.</p>
      </div>
    {%- when 'blue-sapphire' -%}
      <div class="gem-care">
        <p>Blue Sapphire is one of the hardest gemstones in the world — Mohs 9 — which makes it naturally well-suited to daily wear. That said, mindful care keeps it at its best over years of use.</p>
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 16px;">
          <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a3c34; margin-bottom: 10px;">Do</h4>
            <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
              <li>Clean gently with a soft cloth after wear.</li>
              <li>Use lukewarm water and a drop of mild soap occasionally.</li>
              <li>Store separately in a padded box away from harder stones.</li>
              <li>Ensure the setting is secure before wearing regularly.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div style="background: #fff5f5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h4 style="color: #c53030; margin-bottom: 10px;">Avoid</h4>
            <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
              <li>Chemicals, perfumes, and detergents.</li>
              <li>Ultrasonic or steam cleaning.</li>
              <li>Extreme heat and prolonged direct sunlight.</li>
              <li>Remove during heavy physical activity, gym sessions, or contact sports.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 16px; border-left: 4px solid var(--color-gold); margin-top: 20px;">
          <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>On treatments:</strong> Untreated Blue Sapphires are the most valuable and are strongly preferred for astrological use. Heat-treated stones are stable and acceptable when fully disclosed. What is never acceptable — and what we never carry — are glass-filled or diffusion-treated stones. These are unsuitable for astrology, compromise long-term durability, and should always be avoided. An unstable or shifting colour is a clear red flag.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- when 'opal' -%}
      <div class="gem-care">
        <p>Opal is softer than many gemstones and responds best to gentleness. It is not fragile when handled with awareness — but it does not forgive harshness.</p>
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 16px;">
          <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a3c34; margin-bottom: 10px;">Do</h4>
            <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
              <li>Clean gently with a soft cloth after wear.</li>
              <li>Use mild soap and lukewarm water occasionally — for Australian Opals only.</li>
              <li>Store separately in a padded box away from harder stones.</li>
              <li>Ensure the setting is secure, especially in rings.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div style="background: #fff5f5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h4 style="color: #c53030; margin-bottom: 10px;">Avoid</h4>
            <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
              <li>Water contact for Ethiopian Opals — can cause temporary cloudiness.</li>
              <li>Perfumes, lotions, detergents, and alcohol-based products.</li>
              <li>Ultrasonic or steam cleaning.</li>
              <li>Heat and sudden temperature changes.</li>
              <li>Gym sessions, manual work, or any physical impact while wearing.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 16px; border-left: 4px solid var(--color-gold); margin-top: 20px;">
          <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>On treatments:</strong> All our Opals are 100% natural, untreated, and uncoated. What is never acceptable for astrological use — doublets, triplets, wax filling, resin filling, or any composite stone sold as solid. If a stone is not confirmed as solid, natural, untreated, and certified, it should not be purchased for astrological purposes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- when 'ruby' -%}
      <p>Ruby is one of the hardest gemstones in the world — Mohs 9 — and is well suited to daily wear when properly set. It asks only for basic mindfulness, not delicate handling.</p>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 16px;">
        <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
          <h4 style="color: #1a3c34; margin-bottom: 10px;"> Do's</h4>
          <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li>Clean with a soft, lint-free cloth after wear.</li>
            <li>Use lukewarm water and a drop of mild soap occasionally.</li>
            <li>Store separately in a padded box.</li>
            <li>Check prongs or bezels regularly on daily-wear rings.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fff5f5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
          <h4 style="color: #c53030; margin-bottom: 10px;"> Don'ts</h4>
          <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li>Avoid ultrasonic or steam cleaning.</li>
            <li>Keep away from harsh chemicals, acids, perfumes, and detergents.</li>
            <li>Remove during gym, manual work, or contact sports.</li>
            <li>Store away from diamonds and other harder stones.</li>
