        </div>
      </div>
    {%- when 'turquoise' -%}
      <div class="gem-care">
        <p>Turquoise is a porous, sensitive gemstone and the most care-intensive stone in this collection. It is not fragile if treated with real awareness — but it is unforgiving of carelessness. Colour change is irreversible; prevention through consistent care is the only protection.</p>
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 16px;">
          <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a3c34; margin-bottom: 10px;">Do</h4>
            <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
              <li>Clean with a soft, dry cloth after every wear to remove sweat and skin oils.</li>
              <li>Store separately in a padded box, away from moisture, humidity, and harder stones.</li>
              <li>Apply perfumes, deodorants, and cosmetics before putting the stone on — never after.</li>
              <li>Always wear in a protective (bezel or semi-bezel) setting.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div style="background: #fff5f5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;">
            <h4 style="color: #c53030; margin-bottom: 10px;">Avoid</h4>
            <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
              <li>Soaking in water or soap solutions; perfumes, oils, lotions, chemicals.</li>
              <li>Ultrasonic, steam, or chemical cleaning.</li>
              <li>Heat, strong sunlight, and sudden temperature changes.</li>
              <li>Remove before bathing, swimming, gym sessions, or any manual activity.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 16px; border-left: 4px solid var(--color-gold); margin-top: 20px;">
          <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>On colour change:</strong> Turquoise can darken permanently if it absorbs sweat, oils, or chemicals over time — this is not a cleaning issue but a structural one, and it is irreversible. Natural, untreated stones are more susceptible than stabilised ones and require proportionally more care.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- when 'surya' -%}
      <div class="gem-care">
        <p>For Surya (Sun) gemstones — primarily Ruby — care follows the same guidelines as the Ruby collection. Ruby sits at Mohs 9 and is highly durable, but mindful care preserves its colour and surface quality.</p>
        <p>Clean with a soft cloth after wear. Avoid ultrasonic cleaning, harsh chemicals, and prolonged heat. Remove during heavy physical activity. Refer to the Ruby collection for detailed care guidance.</p>
      </div>
    {%- when 'chandra' -%}
      <div class="gem-care">
        <p>For Chandra (Moon) gemstones — primarily Pearl — care requires gentle handling as Pearl is an organic gemstone. Wipe with a soft, dry cloth after every wear. Avoid perfumes, cosmetics, chemicals, and prolonged moisture exposure.</p>
        <p>Store separately in a soft pouch away from harder stones. Remove before sleeping, swimming, or physical activity. Refer to the Pearl collection for detailed care guidance.</p>
      </div>
    {%- when 'mangal' -%}
      <div class="gem-care">
        <p>For Mangal (Mars) gemstones — primarily Red Coral — care requires awareness of its organic, porous nature. Wipe gently with a soft, dry cloth after every wear. Avoid soaking, chemicals, perfumes, and physical impact.</p>
        <p>Store separately in a padded box. Remove before gym sessions, swimming, or manual work. Refer to the Red Coral collection for detailed care guidance.</p>
      </div>
    {%- when 'budh' -%}
